    fix(sem): eliminate parse errors on entire-api and entire.io corpora

    entire graph edges reported ~100 E_PARSE_ERROR partial failures across the
    two production repos. Root causes and fixes, all position-preserving masks:

    SQL (74 files, mostly goose migrations):
    - SET search_path TO a, b — the mask only knew the `=` form; now covers TO
      and consumes the trailing `;` (a bare `;` is itself a parse error).
    - ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES and multi-name DROP (`DROP TABLE IF EXISTS a, b;`)
      masked; a column literally named `key` is rewritten to a non-keyword.
    - Statement patterns matched DDL-looking prose inside comments ("unique
      within a repo", "no partition of relation ...") and their replacements
      stomped bytes of real statements; all patterns now search a comment-free
      view, re-snapshotted after dollar-quoted bodies are blanked so string
      literals like EXECUTE format('... PARTITION OF ...') can't re-trigger.

    TypeScript/TSX (29 files, mostly vitest suites):
    - .tsx got no masking at all; typeof import(...) in generic call args (the
      standard vi.mock/importOriginal pattern) swallowed whole files. A new
      maskTSXUnsupportedSyntax applies the shared rewrites without the .ts-only
      generic-call-signature line masking.
    - Bare import("./x").Foo type references (no typeof), export type * from,
      identifier `unique` after `<` (the unique-symbol keyword), and in_-prefixed
      type members (`in_progress_maintenances:`) all masked.

    Bash:
    - exec 3<>/dev/tcp/... fd-duplex redirections and 10#$var arithmetic base
      literals masked.

    Both repos now stream edges with zero E_PARSE_ERROR partial failures.

